s County shows August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025, on the middle of the grids, January to February ran 31% of normal and November to December 49%. This year so far, March to April came in at 134% of normal for 2026 on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grids 25041, 25042 and 25043 at 48% of normal.</p>"}
